PDP-8a Programmer's Panel
<UL>
<LI><b>board1</b> is the latest drawing of board 1 (front) of the 8/A front
panel replacement.</LI>
<LI><b>board2</b> is the latest drawing of board 2 (back) of the 8/A front
panel replacement.</LI>
<LI><b>board2-4layer</b> is a 4 layer version of board2.</LI>
<LI><b>board2-c</b> is a version of board2 with a different layout (requested by Charles).</LI>
<LI><b>oboard2</b> is a checkpoint of an old version (06/02/2005) of
board2.</LI>
<LI><b>Progpanl.fpd</b> is a Front Panel Express drawing of the Programmer's
Panel artwork.</LI>
<LI><b>nosilkboth.brd</b> is both boards panelized, which is how the prototypes
were ordered.  This version has not had the silkscreen scripts run.</LI>
<LI><b>both.brd</b> is both boards panelized, which is how the prototypes
were ordered.  This version has had the silkscreen scripts run.</LI>
<LI><b>board1-0</b> is a snapshot of revision 0 of board1.</LI>
<LI><b>board2-0</b> is a snapshot of revision 0 of board2.</LI>
<LI><b>board1corrected</b> is board1 with the corrections to make DEC's
schematics work.</LI>
<LI><b>board2corrected</b> is board2 with the first set of corrections to make DEC's
schematics work. (Has a consistency problem to highlight changes.)</LI>
<LI><b>board2eco</b> is board2 with the first and second set of corrections applied to make it work.
(Has a consistency problem which highlights the ECOs.)</LI>
<LI><b>5411507</b> is a drawing of the board inside the limited function panel.</LI>
